    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>I’ve spent my career moving between building, teaching, and leading.</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>I work at the intersection of software engineering, AI and data science, technical education, and product strategy. That mix has made me comfortable moving from a technical problem to a customer conversation to a learning experience — often in the same project.</p>
      <p>I’ve led AI and programming portfolios, built and reviewed technical curriculum, supported enterprise customers, taught working developers and career changers, and worked with teams trying to make sense of a technology landscape that changes faster than most planning cycles.</p>
      <p>I care about technical accuracy, useful learning, and shipping work that survives contact with the real world. I also believe good technical education should respect the learner: explain the hard parts clearly without pretending they are simple.</p>
      <h2>Background</h2>
      <p>My background spans software development, AI and data science, curriculum and product leadership, consulting, and live instruction. I hold a Master of Science in Computer Science and continue to build hands-on projects because staying close to the technology matters.</p>
      <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
      <p>You can find my code on <a href="https://github.com/farishkash">GitHub</a> and my professional history on <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/farishkash/">LinkedIn</a>.</p>
